<title>USA: TABLE-Ply Gem Q2 net income falls.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Ply Gem Q2 net income falls.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>PLY GEM Industries, Inc.</p>
<p>		    Quarter Ended	   Six months ended</p>
<p>		    June 30,   June 30,   June 30,   June 30,</p>
<p>			1997	 1996	 1997	  1996</p>
<p>Net Sales	  $218,916  $212,079   $381,728   $354,097</p>
<p>Merger Costs     $2,850	--	 $2,850	  --</p>
<p>Operating Income $8,611    $10,103    $8,849     $7,220</p>
<p>Net Income	 $3,033    $4,157     $1,980     $1,519</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share</p>
<p>		     $.20	$.28	 $.14	 $.11</p>
<p>Average Shares Outstanding</p>
<p>		   16,586    16,102	13,842     14,251</p>
<p>Excluding Merger Costs</p>
<p>Operating Income $11,461  $10,103   $11,699    $7,220</p>
<p>Net Income	 $4,799   $4,157    $3,746     $1,519</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share</p>
<p>		     $.31     $.28	$.27	 $.11</p>
<p>		(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Co announced on July 24 termination an agreement with Atrium Corporation and, in turn, executed definitive agreements with Nortek, Inc. to be acquired at a price of $19.50 per share.  In its second quarter financial results, PLY GEM recorded merger expenses of $2.9 million, resulting in reported net income for the quarter of $3.0 million, or $0.20 per share.</p>
